### Background and motivation

`MemoryExtension` class offers `ContainsAny{Except}`, `{Last}IndexOfAny{Except}`, and `SplitAny` overloads that accept `SearchValues<T>`. #59466 mentioned that overloads for more methods can be added in the future.

Specifically, I found this operation useful:

> Counting the number of times a specified set of values occur in a given sequence

i.e. `CountOfAny`, which is not available at this time.

It can be helpful for string escaping scenarios: knowing the number of characters that needs escaping allows for right-sizing buffers before the operation.

Users can implement this overload today trivially by lowering into looped `IndexOfAny` calls. But I believe it can be better if offered directly by the BCL:

- Less boilerplate code
- Potential performance optimizations
- Less room for errors, especially if a high-performance implementation is involving

### API Proposal

APIs wanted for my stated use case:

```csharp
namespace System;

public static class MemoryExtensions
{
    public static int CountOfAny<T>(this ReadOnlySpan<T> span, SearchValues<T> values) where T : IEquatable<T>;
    public static int CountOfAny<T>(this ReadOnlySpan<T> span, params ReadOnlySpan<T> values) where T : IEquatable<T>;
}
```

APIs that I don't need at this time and can be added later on-demand, but for completeness:

```csharp
namespace System;

public static class MemoryExtensions
{
    public static int CountOfAnyExcept<T>(this ReadOnlySpan<T> span, SearchValues<T> values) where T : IEquatable<T>;
    public static int CountOfAnyExcept<T>(this ReadOnlySpan<T> span, params ReadOnlySpan<T> values) where T : IEquatable<T>;

    public static void ReplaceAny<T>(this Span<T> span, SearchValues<T> oldValues, T newValue) where T : IEquatable<T>;
    public static void ReplaceAny<T>(this ReadOnlySpan<T> source, Span<T> destination, SearchValues<T> oldValues, T newValue) where T : IEquatable<T>;

    public static ReadOnlySpan<T> Trim<T> (this ReadOnlySpan<T> span, SearchValues<T> trimElements) where T : IEquatable<T>;
    public static ReadOnlyMemory<T> Trim<T> (this ReadOnlyMemory<T> memory, SearchValues<T> trimElements) where T : IEquatable<T>;
}
```

I believe that the upcoming first-class Span feature for C# eliminates the need for `Span<T>` counterparts. But consider them included if that's not the case.


### API Usage

The following method uses the proposed API to escape all eligible characters in a string with [C# escape sequences](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/programming-guide/strings/#string-escape-sequences) (excluding `\u`, `\U`, and `\x`, of course):

```csharp
Debug.Assert(string.Equals(StringExtensions.EscapeForCSharp(null), null, StringComparison.Ordinal));
Debug.Assert(string.Equals("".EscapeForCSharp(), "", StringComparison.Ordinal));
Debug.Assert(string.Equals("Test".EscapeForCSharp(), "Test", StringComparison.Ordinal));
Debug.Assert(string.Equals("\'\"\\\0\a\b\e\f\n\r\t\v".EscapeForCSharp(), @"\'\""\\\0\a\b\e\f\n\r\t\v", StringComparison.Ordinal));
Debug.Assert(string.Equals("\'Test\n".EscapeForCSharp(), @"\'Test\n", StringComparison.Ordinal));
Debug.Assert(string.Equals("Te\tst".EscapeForCSharp(), @"Te\tst", StringComparison.Ordinal));

public static class StringExtensions
{
    [return: NotNullIfNotNull(nameof(original))] 
    public static string? EscapeForCSharp(this string? original)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(original))
        {
            return original;
        }
        ReadOnlySpan<char> originalSpan = original.AsSpan();
        int escapeCount = originalSpan.Count(searchValues);
        if (escapeCount == 0)
        {
            return original;
        }
        int bufferSize = originalSpan.Length + escapeCount;
        return string.Create(bufferSize, originalSpan, (Span<char> buffer, ReadOnlySpan<char> originalSpan) =>
        {
            int writtenChars = 0;
            foreach (Range splitRange in originalSpan.SplitAny(searchValues))
            {
                (int offset, int length) = splitRange.GetOffsetAndLength(originalSpan.Length);
                originalSpan[splitRange].CopyTo(buffer[writtenChars..]);
                writtenChars += length;
                Debug.Assert(offset + length <= originalSpan.Length);
                if (offset + length == originalSpan.Length)
                {
                    break;
                }
                char escapedChar = originalSpan[offset + length];
                ReadOnlySpan<char> escapeSequence = escapedChar switch
                {
                    '\'' => "\\\'",
                    '\"' => "\\\"",
                    '\\' => "\\\\",
                    '\0' => "\\0",
                    '\a' => "\\a",
                    '\b' => "\\b",
                    '\e' => "\\e",
                    '\f' => "\\f",
                    '\n' => "\\n",
                    '\r' => "\\r",
                    '\t' => "\\t",
                    '\v' => "\\v",
                    _ => throw new UnreachableException()
                };
                escapeSequence.CopyTo(buffer[writtenChars..]);
                writtenChars += escapeSequence.Length;
            }
        });
    }

    private static readonly SearchValues<char> searchValues = SearchValues.Create("\'\"\\\0\a\b\e\f\n\r\t\v");
}
```


